runs 'work' on another thread, and it uses the pool (work calls read, line 19: s.fetch()): a PoolManager belongs to one thread, like a global the program changes, so a routine another thread runs can't set it up, add to it, fetch from it, remove from it, sweep it or end it. Keep the entities on one thread, or put a graph that threads share behind a manager such as Guarded, or under an exclusive access
